# fifo_op_async_faults: The asynchronous class (A): a task's completion handler faults the stamp at the offset latched when the command was read, for any status other than 1. Only a service task answers with another status on its own, so this runs under isolation only: task 1's page table root is 0, its first walk kills its service (docs/testing.md, section 5.5), and every later command on it then faults, with 0x103c at its own ring offset, while the root FIFO goes on.
